# Read by Vite at dev/build time. Vite's envDir is `frontend/`, so this file --
# not the repository-root `.env` -- is what defines `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`.
# The app has no hardcoded fallback, so if this is missing the API calls fail
# loudly instead of silently going to the wrong port.
#
# The API runs on port 8001 locally; keep this in step with the `--port` passed
# to uvicorn and with CORS_ORIGINS in the repository-root `.env`.
#
# Use the literal address uvicorn binds (127.0.0.1) rather than `localhost`:
# `localhost` resolves to ::1 first, where nothing is listening, so the browser
# would open a refused connection before falling back to the working one.
VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1
